48 Summer Olympics. Due to the fact that the " [:a {:href "/venues/223"} "Henley"] " could only accommodate a limited number of boats, and the " [:a {:href "/organizations/52"} "International Canoe Federation"] " forbade heats in races of this distance, the competitors began at intervals of 30 seconds. According to the " [:strong {} "Official Report"] ", “[t]his decision, although inevitable, was not popular, since it is impossible for a competitor to judge his position relative to the others, and he is forced to race to the clock, an extremely difficult technique”."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Swedish duo captured the Olympic gold medal, as expected, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/10405"} "Ivar Mathisen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10424"} "Knut Østby"] " of Norway crossing the line next for silver, and Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9523"} "Ture Axelsson"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9525"} "Nils Björklöf"] " taking bronze. Axelsson and Björklöf would go on to win bronze in the " [:a {:href "/results/255031"} "K-2 1,000"] " the following day."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10813"} "Gunnar Åkerlund"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/10811"} "Hans Wetterström"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "46:09.4"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10405"} "Ivar Mathisen"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/10424"} "Knut Østby"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "46:44.8"] [:td {} [:span {:class